# App Color Palette

All new UI elements (components, screens, modals, panels) must be built using
the existing dark navy-indigo palette — don't invent new colors for base
surfaces/text unless the user explicitly asks for a new look.

## Core tokens (`tailwind.config.js` → `theme.extend.colors.dark`)

| Token | Hex | Use for |
|---|---|---|
| `dark-bg` | `#1a1a2e` | App/page background |
| `dark-surface` | `#16213e` | Panels, cards, modal bodies |
| `dark-accent` | `#0f3460` | Borders, dividers, subtle fills, inactive controls |
| `dark-text` | `#e4e4e7` | Primary text |
| `dark-muted` | `#a1a1aa` | Secondary/muted text, placeholders |

Prefer Tailwind utility classes over raw hex: `bg-dark-bg`, `bg-dark-surface`,
`border-dark-accent`, `text-dark-text`, `text-dark-muted`. Use `/NN` opacity
modifiers (e.g. `border-dark-accent/50`, `bg-dark-accent/40`) for hover/disabled
states, matching existing components.

## Interactive accent

- Primary interactive blue: `#3b82f6` (Tailwind `blue-500`), hover `#60a5fa`
  (`blue-400`), active `#2563eb` (`blue-600`). Used for focus rings, checked
  checkboxes/radios, active sliders, "active" nav/tab states.
- Focus rings: `focus:outline-none focus:border-blue-500` or
  `focus:ring-blue-500/50`.

## Status colors

- Success: `green-400` text on `green-500/20` background, `green-500/50` border.
- Error/danger: `red-400` text on `red-500/15` background, `red-500/30` border.

## Guidance

- Match existing component patterns (e.g. `ModeSwitchNavbar`, `ChartsScriptPane`,
  `Button`) rather than introducing one-off styling.
- If a new UI element seems to need a color outside this palette, flag it to
  the user instead of picking one unilaterally.
